---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site } from '../lib/url'
---

<Base title="Privacy & legal notice" current="privacy" description="Privacy statement and legal notice for this website and for Mufaddal Hirani's browser extensions.">
  <div class="wrap narrow page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy &amp; legal notice</p>
    <h1 class="h1">Short, because there’s little to say.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h2">Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}, {site.location}.<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>This is a private, non-commercial portfolio. It sells nothing and carries no advertising.</p>

      <h2 class="h2">What this site collects</h2>
      <p><strong>Nothing.</strong> Specifically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking pixels, no social-media embeds.</li>
        <li>No requests to third parties. Fonts, images and videos are served from this site itself, not from Google Fonts or any CDN.</li>
        <li>If you switch between light and dark mode, that choice is saved in your own browser’s local storage. It never leaves your device, and you can clear it at any time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2">Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages by GitHub, Inc. When you visit, your browser connects to GitHub’s servers,
        which may log technical data such as your IP address for security and to run the service. I have no access
        to those logs. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2">If you email me</h2>
      <p>
        I use your message and address only to reply, and I don’t share them. Ask me at any time to delete our
        correspondence and I will.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" id="extensions">Browser extensions</h2>
      <p>
        This section is the privacy policy for <strong>YouTube Music – Select All</strong> and
        <strong>Just This Video — YouTube Focus Mode</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Neither extension collects, stores, sells or transmits personal data.</li>
        <li>Neither makes any network request of its own. They only change how YouTube pages look and behave in your browser.</li>
        <li>YouTube Music – Select All requests no permissions and stores nothing.</li>
        <li>
          Just This Video stores only its on/off settings with <code>chrome.storage.sync</code>. If you are signed in to
          your browser, your browser vendor syncs those settings between your devices.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {site.updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: clamp(48px, 8vw, 96px); padding-bottom: 40px; }
  .page .h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 36px); }
</style>
